Online auction platform like eBay- Notes

Functional Requirements:
  User persona:
        Buyer, Seller, Anonymous uses.
   Listing for sale can be posted to end at any time in the future up to 30 days from now.
   Should show the highest bid so far for the auction while it is still open
   Can a buyer make multiple bids per product ? (but only 1 active bid at a time)
   Anonymus user can see listing but can not participate in auction.
Bids with same or lower price for the same auction are rejected.
Product info can't be changed after it's published for sale (will need to be unpublished to edit)

Out of scope:
- search
- sign-in-up process
- payments

Non Functional Requirements:
100K daily active users
10K auctions per day
median 100 bids per auction
max 10K bids per auction for all auction duration
max 1K bids per second per auction
1M registred buyers
1K registered sellers
accepting bids: less than 1s for p99
live updates delivery: under 3s for p99
strong consistency for accepting bids
CAP: consistency is preferred
strong consistency for placing bids seen by the bidder;
eventual for other bidders seeing this bid
1 country (e.g. USA), 1 currency

Out of scope:
- GDPR
- disaster recovery

   
API:
// Post or Listing of the product
POST  host/auctions   
{
    sellerId, productTitle, initialPrice, description, exprationDateTime 
}

// Post bid on the auction
POST host/autions{id}/bid  
{
    buyerId, bidPrice
}

Response 200 - if price is greater that current highest price
    For existing Buyer - inactive old big and make new bid active
    For new Buyer - accept the bid if it is higher than current highest bid
Response 400 - if price is matching with any bid or lower than current highest price
                    - if existing bid has buyerId return 400, bid already exist by you.

// Unpublish auction
POST host/autions{id}
{
    action = Unpublish
}

// Update auction details
PUT host/auctions{id}
{
    productTitle, initialPrice, description, exprationDateTime 
}

// Publish auction - Bring it back to market
POST host/autions{id}
{
    action = publish
}

GET host/auctions?status=active&titleContains=''"// Returnes all active the auction

Get host/auctions/{id}/bids/highestBid

// Show details of a specific auction
Get host/auctions/{id} 
Response body
{
    productTitle, initialPrice, description, exprationDateTime 
}

// Show all bids of the specific auction
Get host/auctions/{id}/bids 

